1
00:00:00,016 --> 00:00:01,016
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,016 --> 00:00:02,016
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,016 --> 00:00:03,616
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,616 --> 00:00:06,816
[Episode 12]

5
00:00:16,084 --> 00:00:18,132
Hang on tight.

6
00:00:18,132 --> 00:00:21,283
If you fall, you'll wreck your feet.

7
00:00:50,148 --> 00:00:52,120
Hey, Bong Tae Min.

8
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:54,032
Give me that thing from last time.

9
00:00:54,032 --> 00:00:55,240
What thing?

10
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:57,040
The gun you made.

11
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,749
A gun?

12
00:01:03,896 --> 00:01:05,596
[Deamokjang Milk]

13
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:22,492
Oh.

14
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:26,083
You have good hearing.

15
00:01:26,083 --> 00:01:28,016
What are you doing here all by yourself?

16
00:01:30,848 --> 00:01:32,172
I'm practicing.

17
00:01:32,172 --> 00:01:34,296
I want to get revenge when I grow up.

18
00:01:34,296 --> 00:01:36,164
Revenge?

19
00:01:36,164 --> 00:01:37,396
On whom?

20
00:01:37,396 --> 00:01:39,024
Bad adults.

21
00:01:39,024 --> 00:01:43,649
That's not revenge.
It's called punishing the guilty.

22
00:01:46,683 --> 00:01:50,748
You should target their weakest point.

23
00:01:50,748 --> 00:01:52,448
In one shot.

24
00:01:53,224 --> 00:01:54,983
Right on target.

25
00:02:04,108 --> 00:02:07,216
Oh, impressive.

26
00:02:08,564 --> 00:02:11,420
Brave little girl, what's your name?

27
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:13,072
I'm Yoo Bo Na.

28
00:02:13,072 --> 00:02:14,732
Ma'am, who are you?

29
00:02:14,732 --> 00:02:17,783
Well, who should I say I am?

30
00:02:27,744 --> 00:02:29,444
What is it?

31
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,980
Get inside!

32
00:02:39,012 --> 00:02:40,712
You little...

33
00:02:45,048 --> 00:02:49,549
Kids who bite the hand that feeds
and shelters them

34
00:02:49,549 --> 00:02:53,124
ought to have their lights snuffed out,
don't you think?

35
00:02:55,472 --> 00:02:56,640
Look at this little punk.

36
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:58,051
What are you going to do with that?

37
00:02:58,051 --> 00:02:59,849
Play with me?

38
00:03:04,096 --> 00:03:05,796
Hey!

39
00:03:08,812 --> 00:03:12,183
<i>What? Why are you doing this to me?</i>

40
00:03:30,672 --> 00:03:32,256
<i>All patrol units, attention.</i>

41
00:03:32,256 --> 00:03:34,480
<i>Right outside Ji Hye Pub in downtown
Iseong-dong, Myeongin-gu.</i>

42
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,564
<i>A drunken man has smashed a soju bottle</i>

43
00:03:36,564 --> 00:03:38,924
<i>and is causing a disturbance,
holding a woman hostage.</i>

44
00:03:38,924 --> 00:03:42,083
- <i>Nearby patrol cars, dispatch now.</i>
- Iseong-dong is right next door.

45
00:03:43,312 --> 00:03:45,228
<i>There are currently no available patrol cars.</i>

46
00:03:45,228 --> 00:03:47,252
<i>Including nearby detectives and mobile units,</i>

47
00:03:47,252 --> 00:03:48,772
<i>all available units, please respond.</i>

48
00:03:48,772 --> 00:03:51,783
Oh, looks like there aren't
any patrol cars nearby.

49
00:03:52,948 --> 00:03:54,408
<i>The situation at the scene is escalating.</i>

50
00:03:54,408 --> 00:03:58,076
<i>Nearest available unit, regardless of
assignment, respond immediately.</i>

51
00:03:58,076 --> 00:04:00,010
- Hey, Beom, let's roll.
- Alright.

52
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:01,088
Two detectives from the Nambu Police Station,

53
00:04:01,088 --> 00:04:03,783
currently staking out near Iseong-dong,
are responding to the scene.

54
00:04:21,436 --> 00:04:24,676
<i>Ms. Bo Na, please stop!</i>

55
00:04:24,676 --> 00:04:27,136
He's already unconscious, Ms. Yoo!

56
00:04:27,136 --> 00:04:28,836
Ms. Yoo!

57
00:04:33,012 --> 00:04:34,944
Yoo Bo Na.

58
00:04:34,944 --> 00:04:36,683
<i>Stop it now.</i>

59
00:04:40,144 --> 00:04:41,849
Director Yoo.

60
00:04:43,047 --> 00:04:44,949
Are you okay?

61
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:59,683
Did you really not report
a drunken disturbance?

62
00:04:59,683 --> 00:05:01,488
A drunken disturbance?

63
00:05:01,488 --> 00:05:03,849
I never made such a report.

64
00:05:03,849 --> 00:05:04,849
What?

65
00:05:04,849 --> 00:05:10,244
Wait. Didn't a drunk man smash
a soju bottle and threaten a woman?

66
00:05:10,244 --> 00:05:12,496
No. Nothing like that happened.

67
00:05:12,496 --> 00:05:15,249
Are you sure you have the right place?

68
00:05:21,864 --> 00:05:23,583
Darn it.

69
00:05:24,636 --> 00:05:26,549
<i>We've got a witness.</i>

70
00:05:27,592 --> 00:05:30,583
Why is a child who should be
in protective care even here?

71
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:58,316
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

72
00:06:00,076 --> 00:06:04,032
We're here to help you out.

73
00:06:04,032 --> 00:06:06,976
Get a good night's sleep.

74
00:06:06,976 --> 00:06:09,949
Tomorrow will be a new day.

75
00:06:32,417 --> 00:06:34,220
<i>Someone has collapsed and is bleeding
from the head on the fifth floor</i>

76
00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:36,820
<i>of the emergency stairs at King Tower.</i>

77
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:39,049
<i>I think he's going to die
if you don't get here quickly.</i>

78
00:06:45,025 --> 00:06:46,476
Excuse me!

79
00:06:46,476 --> 00:06:49,376
Have we met before?

80
00:06:49,376 --> 00:06:51,024
No.

81
00:06:51,024 --> 00:06:54,249
Oh, it's dangerous
to touch it that carelessly...

82
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,456
How was your first day back at work?
Was it tough?

83
00:06:59,456 --> 00:07:01,949
It's something I've done for a long time,
so it came back quickly.

84
00:07:01,949 --> 00:07:05,796
<i>Some speculate that Kingfisher,
the infamous serial gun killer</i>

85
00:07:05,796 --> 00:07:07,300
<i>who disappeared for the past four years...</i>

86
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:09,524
Didn't you have a client meeting today?
Did it not go well?

87
00:07:09,524 --> 00:07:13,332
Oh, the meeting fell through this afternoon,
so it got pushed to tonight.

88
00:07:13,332 --> 00:07:14,949
[Kingfisher Strikes Again]
<i>This is the first time</i>

89
00:07:14,949 --> 00:07:17,183
[Two Casino VIP Guests Killed]
<i>two people have been killed</i>

90
00:07:17,183 --> 00:07:19,636
<i>in a single Kingfisher case.</i>

91
00:07:19,636 --> 00:07:21,512
<i>I like you, Bo Na.</i>

92
00:07:21,512 --> 00:07:24,383
You don't really know much about me, do you?

93
00:08:27,564 --> 00:08:29,264
Gu Jong Ryeol!

94
00:08:32,032 --> 00:08:34,816
What? Has someone already called it in?

95
00:08:42,844 --> 00:08:45,228
I'm Detective Lee Dong Jin
from Nambu Station. What's going on?

96
00:08:45,228 --> 00:08:47,916
We received a report that
a sick child is home alone.

97
00:08:47,916 --> 00:08:49,616
I believe this is the house.

98
00:08:57,972 --> 00:09:01,528
For the seven years my dad was in prison,

99
00:09:01,528 --> 00:09:05,588
everyone at school
called me an idiot or a freak.

100
00:09:05,588 --> 00:09:08,224
I was always spaced out.

101
00:09:08,224 --> 00:09:12,883
Even the slightest sound,
like a pen dropping, would make me jump.

102
00:09:14,096 --> 00:09:16,748
<i>If someone even brushed past my shoulder,</i>

103
00:09:16,748 --> 00:09:19,316
I'd collapse and tremble.

104
00:09:20,828 --> 00:09:25,504
The doctors said I'd be fine
and get better with time,

105
00:09:25,504 --> 00:09:27,583
but I never did.

106
00:09:28,484 --> 00:09:30,983
One day, I realized why.

107
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:33,960
Because Dad would be...

108
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:37,283
coming back in a few years.

109
00:09:38,724 --> 00:09:41,483
Because it wasn't over yet.

110
00:09:42,516 --> 00:09:46,449
When I watched my dad disappear
right before my eyes,

111
00:09:47,092 --> 00:09:48,916
<i>I thought to myself.</i>

112
00:09:50,972 --> 00:09:52,983
<i>"It's finally over."</i>

113
00:09:55,296 --> 00:09:57,649
<i>"Maybe now I can live...</i>

114
00:09:59,749 --> 00:10:02,176
<i>a normal life,</i>

115
00:10:02,176 --> 00:10:04,249
like everyone else."

116
00:10:05,236 --> 00:10:08,283
Today will probably be
that kind of day for that girl.

117
00:10:09,852 --> 00:10:12,083
The day she's freed from violence.

118
00:10:30,528 --> 00:10:31,771
Save me.

119
00:10:31,771 --> 00:10:35,236
Well... Ugh...

120
00:10:35,236 --> 00:10:37,276
The inhaler... The...

121
00:10:37,276 --> 00:10:39,583
The inhaler... My inhaler, please.

122
00:10:39,583 --> 00:10:41,036
The inhaler...

123
00:10:41,036 --> 00:10:42,849
Please, the inhaler...

124
00:10:46,076 --> 00:10:49,200
Please... Please save me...

125
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,949
Save me. Save...

126
00:11:01,636 --> 00:11:05,349
I'm so sorry I got here so late.

127
00:11:10,732 --> 00:11:14,016
I'll take care of the rest.

128
00:11:37,683 --> 00:11:42,276
Your friends will all go somewhere safe.

129
00:11:42,276 --> 00:11:44,552
You're the one who saved those children.

130
00:11:44,552 --> 00:11:47,249
<i>The reason I do this work.</i>

131
00:12:04,688 --> 00:12:07,216
<i>I hope at least one person can be saved,</i>

132
00:12:08,024 --> 00:12:12,049
<i>and someone can be safe because of it.</i>

133
00:12:46,884 --> 00:12:48,584
Tae Seong.

134
00:12:59,544 --> 00:13:01,244
Honey.

135
00:13:02,476 --> 00:13:04,176
Tae Seong.

136
00:13:13,869 --> 00:13:15,324
<i>Hello?</i>

137
00:13:15,324 --> 00:13:18,116
Where are you now, Tae Seong?

138
00:13:25,069 --> 00:13:26,769
Honey!

139
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:32,120
Yul!

140
00:13:32,732 --> 00:13:35,316
What's wrong with Yul? Huh?

141
00:13:36,996 --> 00:13:39,140
Her fever suddenly spiked
while she was sleeping.

142
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:41,340
They say it's the fever cold
that's been going around lately.

143
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:44,564
A cold? She was fine this morning. How did...

144
00:13:44,564 --> 00:13:48,848
So did they say she'll be okay? Huh? Huh?

145
00:13:48,848 --> 00:13:52,172
Her fever broke. They said to monitor her
for a day or two with medication.

146
00:13:52,172 --> 00:13:55,324
She's so tiny, and now...

147
00:13:55,324 --> 00:13:58,416
Yul, you must've been in so much pain, huh?

148
00:14:00,692 --> 00:14:03,048
Oh, poor baby, Yul.

149
00:14:03,048 --> 00:14:06,128
Oh, no, you must've been hurting so much.

150
00:14:06,128 --> 00:14:08,316
Oh, they had to put that
on such a little kid...

151
00:14:10,383 --> 00:14:14,583
Oh, no. I'm sorry Mommy got here so late.

152
00:14:35,556 --> 00:14:39,149
I'll stay by Yul's side tonight.
You go get some rest.

153
00:14:42,848 --> 00:14:46,883
I'll take the day off tomorrow
and stay with Yul, honey.

154
00:14:48,292 --> 00:14:49,992
Okay, then.

155
00:15:00,116 --> 00:15:04,449
[Yul's Room]

156
00:15:54,116 --> 00:15:56,549
[Breaking News: Child Abuser
Gu Jong Ryeol Found Dead Last Night]

157
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,900
Last night...

158
00:16:06,416 --> 00:16:09,583
[Big Precious]

159
00:16:16,783 --> 00:16:19,516
[Big Precious]

160
00:16:38,904 --> 00:16:41,080
[Big Precious]
<i>Honey, when did you leave?</i>

161
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:42,828
<i>You should've woken me.</i>

162
00:16:42,828 --> 00:16:45,508
<i>I would've made you some toast.</i>

163
00:16:45,508 --> 00:16:47,908
<i>Did you take your umbrella?</i>

164
00:16:47,908 --> 00:16:50,141
<i>My husband can't get caught in the rain.</i>

165
00:16:50,141 --> 00:16:51,901
Oh, my...

166
00:17:11,396 --> 00:17:16,696
It seems there are still a lot of things
you don't know about Bo Na.

167
00:17:16,696 --> 00:17:17,996
Oh.

168
00:17:17,996 --> 00:17:20,483
Or does she just not tell you
much about herself?

169
00:17:24,032 --> 00:17:27,116
Yes, Manager Kim. I'm Kwon Tae Seong,
a reporter from Not Today.

170
00:17:27,116 --> 00:17:29,316
Hello. How have you been?

171
00:17:29,316 --> 00:17:31,008
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

172
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:35,428
This case is definitely different
from the pattern we've seen so far.

173
00:17:35,428 --> 00:17:39,688
It's the first time we've found evidence
that the killer physically intervened.

174
00:17:39,688 --> 00:17:43,492
The use of violence suggests
some emotion was involved.

175
00:17:43,492 --> 00:17:46,952
Well, the more enraged you are,
the more times you tend to stab someone.

176
00:17:46,952 --> 00:17:49,516
The fact that they called
an ambulance to report a sick child

177
00:17:49,516 --> 00:17:52,704
also shows that even amid all those emotions,

178
00:17:52,704 --> 00:17:55,383
they clearly wanted to protect the child.

179
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:58,760
Which means...

180
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:02,060
What is this, a funeral? Why the long faces?

181
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:03,949
- Welcome, sir.
- Welcome, sir.

182
00:18:05,359 --> 00:18:08,491
I'm sorry. I should've been more careful.

183
00:18:08,491 --> 00:18:10,380
I let my guard down.

184
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,572
What are you sorry for?

185
00:18:11,572 --> 00:18:14,683
Anyway, we've confirmed that
your theory was right.

186
00:18:14,683 --> 00:18:15,683
Haven't we?

187
00:18:15,683 --> 00:18:17,749
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, that's right.

188
00:18:19,196 --> 00:18:20,504
[Lee Dong Jin]

189
00:18:20,504 --> 00:18:25,092
Don't get down just because Kingfisher
got away this time. Keep at it.

190
00:18:25,092 --> 00:18:28,296
Next time, I'll get the chief to give us
all the support we need,

191
00:18:28,296 --> 00:18:29,844
even if I have to beg him for it.

192
00:18:29,844 --> 00:18:31,602
Got it?

193
00:18:31,602 --> 00:18:32,602
Got it?

194
00:18:32,602 --> 00:18:34,483
- Yes, sir.
- Understood, sir.

195
00:18:36,196 --> 00:18:37,200
You haven't had lunch, right?

196
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:39,916
Use the department credit card
and treat yourself to something nice.

197
00:18:41,216 --> 00:18:43,180
Answer me.

198
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:45,388
- We'll enjoy it.
- Thank you, sir.

199
00:18:45,388 --> 00:18:48,716
I expected him to be strict,
but he's actually pretty chill.

200
00:18:50,444 --> 00:18:52,784
He's been part of the task force
two times before.

201
00:18:52,784 --> 00:18:55,016
Both times, it ended badly,
and he was furious about it.

202
00:18:55,016 --> 00:18:58,683
He's probably the one among us
who wants to catch Kingfisher the most.

203
00:18:58,683 --> 00:19:00,783
[Team Leader Gu Tae Seok]

204
00:19:02,849 --> 00:19:05,588
<i>But there's one thing
that doesn't quite add up.</i>

205
00:19:05,588 --> 00:19:07,780
The false dispatch order
that came into the scene.

206
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,428
We sent it to the voice analysis team,

207
00:19:09,428 --> 00:19:13,140
and they say it was AI-generated,
not a real person's voice.

208
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:16,732
It looks like our police network was hacked.

209
00:19:16,732 --> 00:19:18,784
Hacked?

210
00:19:18,784 --> 00:19:20,072
What does that mean, then?

211
00:19:20,072 --> 00:19:23,183
Did they know we were coming and diverted us?

212
00:19:23,183 --> 00:19:25,156
How?

213
00:19:25,156 --> 00:19:29,444
Could there be a Kingfisher operative
inside the police?

214
00:19:29,444 --> 00:19:32,249
You know, like an undercover operative.

215
00:19:33,784 --> 00:19:38,036
[The Kingfisher Case Files]
<i>It doesn't have to be someone in the police.</i>

216
00:19:38,036 --> 00:19:40,168
<i>I heard Kingfisher's fan cafe alone</i>

217
00:19:40,168 --> 00:19:43,216
<i>has over a million members, right?</i>

218
00:19:49,308 --> 00:19:52,416
<i>Should prison</i>

219
00:19:52,416 --> 00:19:56,024
be a hideout for criminals? Huh?

220
00:19:56,024 --> 00:20:01,496
We're already overcrowded as it is,
running out of space,

221
00:20:01,496 --> 00:20:03,249
aren't we?

222
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,308
<i>Who knows?</i>

223
00:20:07,308 --> 00:20:08,849
<i>Among them could be someone
consumed by vengeance</i>

224
00:20:08,849 --> 00:20:11,283
[Durumi Electronics]
<i>after losing family to a criminal.</i>

225
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:16,624
<i>Maybe...</i>

226
00:20:16,624 --> 00:20:19,883
<i>helpers like that are hiding in places
we never see.</i>

227
00:20:19,883 --> 00:20:21,583
[No Entry to Above-Ground Parking]

228
00:20:26,216 --> 00:20:27,760
Oh, wow!

229
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:30,156
Wow, it's green!

230
00:20:30,156 --> 00:20:34,264
It's done. Once you finish your porridge,
you'll feel better in no time, right?

231
00:20:34,264 --> 00:20:36,764
Yeah, I'll eat lots.

232
00:20:36,764 --> 00:20:39,416
You will? Eat plenty.

233
00:20:46,812 --> 00:20:48,824
Did it hurt when you got the shot?

234
00:20:48,824 --> 00:20:50,728
Yeah, it hurt.

235
00:20:50,728 --> 00:20:53,076
But Daddy hugged me tight.

236
00:20:53,076 --> 00:20:54,436
He did?

237
00:20:54,436 --> 00:20:57,744
Yul, were you sad because Mommy wasn't there?

238
00:20:57,744 --> 00:21:00,760
Yeah, I cried because I missed you.

239
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:04,683
I asked Daddy to call you, but he wouldn't.

240
00:21:05,912 --> 00:21:07,664
He did?

241
00:21:07,664 --> 00:21:08,664
Why would Daddy do that?

242
00:21:08,664 --> 00:21:09,780
I don't know.

243
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:11,480
Eat up.

244
00:21:58,816 --> 00:22:01,016
Back then...

245
00:22:01,016 --> 00:22:03,416
the person who was on the rooftop
beyond that door...

246
00:22:06,984 --> 00:22:08,783
was it Yoo Bo Na?

247
00:22:09,868 --> 00:22:13,583
Looks like you didn't sleep.
Your face looks haggard.

248
00:22:14,476 --> 00:22:17,183
The person you tried to hide that day...

249
00:22:20,024 --> 00:22:21,949
was it Yoo Bo Na?

250
00:22:24,556 --> 00:22:26,256
Good grief.

251
00:22:27,532 --> 00:22:31,249
Why are you walking around in the rain?
You'll catch a cold.

252
00:22:42,452 --> 00:22:45,183
So you finally opened the door.

253
00:22:51,504 --> 00:22:53,792
But that's strange.

254
00:22:53,792 --> 00:22:56,160
Why come to me and ask about it?

255
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:58,049
The person involved is right there.

256
00:22:59,849 --> 00:23:03,683
Were you afraid she'd kill you if you asked?

257
00:23:06,832 --> 00:23:08,532
Are you upset?

258
00:23:09,749 --> 00:23:13,340
Well, I suppose you have
every right to be angry.

259
00:23:13,340 --> 00:23:18,224
After all those years of marriage,
she completely deceived her own husband.

260
00:23:18,224 --> 00:23:21,183
And she hid such a terrifying secret.

261
00:23:22,883 --> 00:23:25,876
That's just how Yoo Bo Na is.

262
00:23:25,876 --> 00:23:29,668
She's that meticulous and shrewd.

263
00:23:29,668 --> 00:23:34,460
She wouldn't even bat an eye
at making a fool out of someone.

264
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:36,160
Shut up.

265
00:23:37,888 --> 00:23:41,212
I'm taking your side right now,
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

266
00:23:41,212 --> 00:23:43,983
What do you know to be talking like that?

267
00:23:45,183 --> 00:23:48,816
Say one more thing like that,
and I won't let you off.

268
00:24:23,328 --> 00:24:26,016
I heard the child was
in a protective shelter.

269
00:24:26,016 --> 00:24:28,064
What happened yesterday?

270
00:24:28,064 --> 00:24:33,312
We have no choice but to release
a child when the parents request it.

271
00:24:33,312 --> 00:24:36,368
At the time, the adoptive mom
was considered the main culprit,

272
00:24:36,368 --> 00:24:39,652
so we had no grounds
to deny the dad's request.

273
00:24:39,652 --> 00:24:44,624
Would it be possible for us
to speak with the child?

274
00:24:44,624 --> 00:24:47,728
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
that's not possible.

275
00:24:47,728 --> 00:24:50,400
The child's doctor stressed that

276
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:52,992
her physical and emotional
well-being has to come first.

277
00:24:52,992 --> 00:24:54,692
I see.

278
00:25:02,728 --> 00:25:06,983
So that punk was abusing
the child again all that time.

279
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:10,700
Could Kingfisher
have witnessed the abuse live?

280
00:25:10,700 --> 00:25:13,144
Could that be why he beat him so brutally?
He saw it and lost his temper?

281
00:25:13,144 --> 00:25:15,249
It's possible.

282
00:25:15,249 --> 00:25:18,196
Oh, then the kid must've seen something.

283
00:25:18,196 --> 00:25:21,788
If you were her, would you tell us?

284
00:25:21,788 --> 00:25:23,716
Actually, I wouldn't either.

285
00:25:23,716 --> 00:25:26,324
He saved her life. She'd owe him
for the rest of her life.

286
00:25:26,324 --> 00:25:27,949
You said that other kid
didn't say anything either.

287
00:25:27,949 --> 00:25:30,016
The one whose dad died on Christmas.

288
00:25:32,120 --> 00:25:33,783
<i>The daughter's name was 'Oh' something.</i>

289
00:25:33,783 --> 00:25:35,483
Wait a second.

290
00:25:37,832 --> 00:25:39,532
Oh Seung Ah.

291
00:25:40,983 --> 00:25:43,080
Let's look for Oh Seung Ah.

292
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:45,583
What? Her?

293
00:25:45,583 --> 00:25:47,349
So far, there have been exactly

294
00:25:47,349 --> 00:25:50,236
two people at Kingfisher
crime scenes who weren't victims.

295
00:25:50,236 --> 00:25:52,080
Yeon Chang Bok's son must still be young.

296
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:54,320
And Oh Seung Ah would be an adult by now.

297
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:55,964
Who knows?

298
00:25:55,964 --> 00:25:59,176
As you said, maybe she's repaying
Kingfisher for saving her.

299
00:25:59,176 --> 00:26:00,456
Let's find her.

300
00:26:00,456 --> 00:26:03,149
Oh, genius!

301
00:26:08,228 --> 00:26:10,296
- Hey!
- Oh, you're here?

302
00:26:10,296 --> 00:26:11,896
Oh, I'm exhausted.

303
00:26:11,896 --> 00:26:14,349
Hey, he's pretty drunk.

304
00:26:20,436 --> 00:26:22,183
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong?

305
00:26:25,516 --> 00:26:29,204
What are you doing here all by yourself,
looking so miserable?

306
00:26:29,204 --> 00:26:31,128
What? Why do you look like a mess?

307
00:26:31,128 --> 00:26:32,483
Reporter Go!

308
00:26:32,483 --> 00:26:36,752
Go Ji Soon! My dear colleague, Go Ji Soon.

309
00:26:36,752 --> 00:26:38,583
- Go Ji Soon!
- Hey, what's wrong with you?

310
00:26:38,583 --> 00:26:40,516
- Go Ji Soon!
- Sit down. Sit down.

311
00:26:40,516 --> 00:26:43,192
Hey, the Chief is really mad.

312
00:26:43,192 --> 00:26:46,660
Hey, you always turned me down
when I asked you to drink,

313
00:26:46,660 --> 00:26:48,532
saying you missed your wife, huh?

314
00:26:48,532 --> 00:26:52,483
And now you're drinking all by yourself?

315
00:26:54,316 --> 00:26:56,249
Did you two have a marital spat?

316
00:26:58,724 --> 00:27:00,816
What's that?

317
00:27:02,216 --> 00:27:04,736
How do you even have one?

318
00:27:04,736 --> 00:27:06,283
You're annoying.

319
00:27:06,283 --> 00:27:08,372
Oh, you're so annoying.

320
00:27:08,372 --> 00:27:12,616
Hey, do you really love your wife that much?

321
00:27:16,312 --> 00:27:17,880
- I do.
- What do you like about her?

322
00:27:17,880 --> 00:27:20,900
What's so great about her?

323
00:27:20,900 --> 00:27:22,983
My wife

324
00:27:22,983 --> 00:27:27,749
can climb rough mountain trails
like it's nothing.

325
00:27:27,749 --> 00:27:30,816
Even when the snow stacks up
as tall as you are,

326
00:27:30,816 --> 00:27:33,977
she plows through like an excavator.

327
00:27:33,977 --> 00:27:40,088
And she's incredibly strong,
so she can lift me right off the ground.

328
00:27:40,088 --> 00:27:43,952
And she's a great shot.

329
00:27:43,952 --> 00:27:46,583
She's not your wife. She's a superhero.

330
00:27:52,616 --> 00:27:56,083
It was our first date in Seoul.

331
00:27:57,784 --> 00:28:00,983
When I asked where she wanted to go,

332
00:28:00,983 --> 00:28:06,283
she just wanted to eat tteokbokki
on the street and buy a hair tie.

333
00:28:06,996 --> 00:28:11,849
When I asked why she
wanted to do those things,

334
00:28:11,849 --> 00:28:15,436
she said she just wanted to
experience those ordinary things.

335
00:28:15,436 --> 00:28:17,724
What kind of cheesy story is that?

336
00:28:17,724 --> 00:28:20,016
When she was pregnant with Yul,

337
00:28:20,964 --> 00:28:22,708
she had really bad morning sickness.

338
00:28:22,708 --> 00:28:24,849
So after work every day,

339
00:28:24,849 --> 00:28:28,183
I got some strawberries
and mixed them with ice for her.

340
00:28:28,916 --> 00:28:32,440
My wife really loves strawberry shakes.

341
00:28:32,440 --> 00:28:34,304
Do you know what she said to me once?

342
00:28:34,304 --> 00:28:36,408
What?

343
00:28:36,408 --> 00:28:39,083
"At this rate, am I going to
give birth to a strawberry?"

344
00:28:42,792 --> 00:28:44,492
Isn't that funny?

345
00:28:46,364 --> 00:28:50,449
Man, you're really rubbing salt
in this old bachelor's wounds.

346
00:28:52,232 --> 00:28:54,312
So?

347
00:28:54,312 --> 00:28:56,012
Are you happy?

348
00:28:59,084 --> 00:29:00,784
I am.

349
00:29:02,248 --> 00:29:05,016
I'm so happy that I could go crazy.

350
00:29:06,928 --> 00:29:08,916
Jeez.

351
00:29:13,816 --> 00:29:16,008
Where are you going?

352
00:29:16,008 --> 00:29:17,816
To see my wife.

353
00:29:36,148 --> 00:29:37,848
You're back?

354
00:29:39,148 --> 00:29:42,583
Why'd you drink so much? Huh?

355
00:29:56,672 --> 00:29:58,372
Well...

356
00:30:00,684 --> 00:30:03,049
I'll get you some honey water, honey.

357
00:30:08,320 --> 00:30:10,983
Honey, drink this. It's honey water.

358
00:30:11,644 --> 00:30:13,344
Okay?

359
00:30:14,796 --> 00:30:17,040
We're married, right?

360
00:30:17,040 --> 00:30:19,372
Of course, we are.

361
00:30:19,372 --> 00:30:21,668
Drink this and sober up a little.

362
00:30:21,668 --> 00:30:25,916
You're my wife, and I'm your husband.

363
00:30:27,540 --> 00:30:30,883
You're Yul's mom, and I'm Yul's dad.

364
00:30:32,320 --> 00:30:34,020
That's what it is.

365
00:30:38,812 --> 00:30:40,512
Right?

366
00:30:43,556 --> 00:30:46,283
Honey, did something happen today?

367
00:30:46,283 --> 00:30:49,349
You haven't answered your phone all day.
What's wrong?

368
00:30:55,796 --> 00:30:58,322
I'm asking because I'm genuinely curious.

369
00:30:58,322 --> 00:31:00,749
Please give me an honest answer.

370
00:31:01,934 --> 00:31:03,600
Okay.

371
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:05,849
What do you want to know?

372
00:31:05,849 --> 00:31:07,549
Do you...

373
00:31:10,652 --> 00:31:14,116
Do you really like strawberry shakes?

374
00:31:16,932 --> 00:31:18,983
Is that really true?

375
00:31:23,216 --> 00:31:25,116
Are you really Yoo Bo Na...

376
00:31:25,952 --> 00:31:29,649
You are, right?
You're really Yoo Bo Na, right?

377
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:36,549
You seem really drunk. Let's go to bed.

378
00:31:40,752 --> 00:31:42,949
What am I to you?

379
00:31:45,208 --> 00:31:48,404
Are you angry with me about something, honey?

380
00:31:48,404 --> 00:31:52,983
Is this because I came home late
without calling yesterday?

381
00:31:52,983 --> 00:31:55,116
Why did you marry me?

382
00:32:00,816 --> 00:32:02,949
Did you really love me?

383
00:32:59,728 --> 00:33:03,583
I actually don't really like
strawberry shakes.

384
00:33:04,620 --> 00:33:06,320
They're too cold.

385
00:33:07,124 --> 00:33:12,283
But when I fell in love,
I really wanted to do that.

386
00:33:13,183 --> 00:33:16,083
Sitting across from each other
and drinking strawberry shakes.

387
00:33:19,328 --> 00:33:21,983
So I just pretended to like them.

388
00:33:24,752 --> 00:33:28,016
Because I wanted to keep doing that with you.

389
00:33:29,820 --> 00:33:33,183
I just loved those moments so much.

390
00:33:37,100 --> 00:33:39,849
Because that's the kind of
person you are to me.

391
00:35:00,268 --> 00:35:02,616
Hey, stop right there!

392
00:35:04,268 --> 00:35:05,968
Oh, there you go again.

393
00:35:07,948 --> 00:35:09,648
What is it?

394
00:35:11,812 --> 00:35:14,088
<i>Have you eaten?</i>

395
00:35:14,088 --> 00:35:16,616
<i>You didn't just snack your way
through another meal, did you?</i>

396
00:35:21,049 --> 00:35:25,183
<i>I ate! Two full bowls of rice
with kimchi stew.</i>

397
00:35:26,244 --> 00:35:27,752
<i>Good job.</i>

398
00:35:27,752 --> 00:35:30,049
<i>Make sure you eat dinner too.</i>

399
00:35:33,964 --> 00:35:35,016
<i>Kwon Se Ah.</i>

400
00:35:35,016 --> 00:35:37,516
I really do like you,

401
00:35:37,516 --> 00:35:40,049
and I was a little upset that
I couldn't see you.

402
00:35:40,049 --> 00:35:43,783
So I'd like you to reply when I text you.

403
00:35:47,196 --> 00:35:49,249
<i>Have you eaten? Eat real food, not ramyeon.</i>

404
00:35:49,249 --> 00:35:50,324
<i>I ate!</i>

405
00:35:50,324 --> 00:35:51,848
<i>Good. What did you eat for lunch?</i>

406
00:35:51,848 --> 00:35:53,316
<i>I mixed tuna with rice.</i>

407
00:35:53,316 --> 00:35:55,140
<i>Oh, sounds good. I'm having dinner.</i>

408
00:35:55,140 --> 00:35:56,883
<i>Have you eaten? Enjoy your meal.</i>

409
00:35:56,883 --> 00:35:59,684
Why are you doing this to me?

410
00:35:59,684 --> 00:36:01,700
Is this the only reason
you asked me to respond?

411
00:36:01,700 --> 00:36:04,683
Are you like a meal-tracking robot or what?

412
00:36:05,716 --> 00:36:07,083
Oh, come on!

413
00:36:07,083 --> 00:36:10,016
I've already eaten! Quit it!

414
00:36:10,016 --> 00:36:12,104
<i>Se Ah, what are you doing tomorrow?</i>

415
00:36:12,104 --> 00:36:14,716
- Oh!
- <i>Shall we meet up?</i>

416
00:36:15,383 --> 00:36:17,583
<i>Is there anywhere you'd like to go?</i>

417
00:36:17,583 --> 00:36:20,016
Yes, yes, yes!

418
00:36:25,968 --> 00:36:27,276
Wow, they're so pretty.

419
00:36:27,276 --> 00:36:28,656
Hello!

420
00:36:28,656 --> 00:36:30,883
Look at its eyes. So pretty.

421
00:36:30,883 --> 00:36:32,283
Come here.

422
00:36:32,283 --> 00:36:34,308
Hello.

423
00:36:34,308 --> 00:36:40,296
Because horses evolved
while being chased by predators,

424
00:36:40,296 --> 00:36:44,220
they can be extremely sensitive to
unfamiliar environments or sudden stimuli...

425
00:36:44,220 --> 00:36:45,940
Let's give it a try, okay?

426
00:36:45,940 --> 00:36:48,468
Sir, can we ride this?

427
00:36:48,468 --> 00:36:51,272
I've never ridden anything except in a car...

428
00:36:51,272 --> 00:36:53,016
Se Ah!

429
00:36:53,016 --> 00:36:54,908
Up you go.

430
00:36:54,908 --> 00:36:56,908
Wow, it's really high.

431
00:36:56,908 --> 00:36:58,144
- Is it fun?
- Yeah.

432
00:36:58,144 --> 00:36:59,683
- Come on, get on.
- No, I'm fine.

433
00:36:59,683 --> 00:37:01,388
He's going to ride too.

434
00:37:01,388 --> 00:37:03,088
I'm fine.

435
00:37:06,908 --> 00:37:09,283
You're... really good at it.

436
00:37:10,040 --> 00:37:11,740
How is it?

437
00:37:15,848 --> 00:37:18,549
- Wow, careful.
- This is amazing.

438
00:37:28,616 --> 00:37:30,728
How did they even ride this?

439
00:37:30,728 --> 00:37:33,016
With the growing emphasis on
low-carbon green growth,

440
00:37:33,016 --> 00:37:35,628
bicycle culture is becoming
increasingly popular...

441
00:37:35,628 --> 00:37:38,749
Wow, let's ride bikes too.

442
00:37:39,583 --> 00:37:42,016
Well, but I've only ever
driven large vehicles...

443
00:37:42,780 --> 00:37:45,420
Assistant Manager Ki, you need to pedal.

444
00:37:45,420 --> 00:37:47,149
Okay?

445
00:37:50,392 --> 00:37:52,149
Fun, right?

446
00:37:56,072 --> 00:37:57,849
It's really nice, right?

447
00:38:07,416 --> 00:38:09,149
[Mr. Tiger]

448
00:38:11,132 --> 00:38:13,816
<i>Did you eat lunch? What'd you have?</i>

449
00:38:14,456 --> 00:38:17,049
<i>I ate jjamppong.</i>

450
00:38:20,756 --> 00:38:23,792
Can I ask you something?

451
00:38:23,792 --> 00:38:25,083
What is it?

452
00:38:25,083 --> 00:38:29,849
What do women like men to say to them?

453
00:38:29,849 --> 00:38:34,024
Something that'll move
a relationship along quickly?

454
00:38:34,024 --> 00:38:35,900
Why bother saying something long?

455
00:38:35,900 --> 00:38:38,116
One sentence is enough.

456
00:38:38,116 --> 00:38:39,816
One sentence?

457
00:38:41,568 --> 00:38:43,364
Ms. Kwon Se Ah.

458
00:38:43,364 --> 00:38:44,628
Yes?

459
00:38:44,628 --> 00:38:46,496
- I love you.
- Yes.

460
00:38:46,496 --> 00:38:48,196
What?

461
00:38:49,016 --> 00:38:51,349
<i>Did I hear that wrong?</i>

462
00:38:51,349 --> 00:38:53,349
You heard me right.

463
00:38:54,080 --> 00:38:55,564
I love you, Se Ah.

464
00:38:55,564 --> 00:38:56,800
What?

465
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:58,500
Why?

466
00:38:59,244 --> 00:39:01,176
You don't like hearing that?

467
00:39:01,176 --> 00:39:02,664
Oh, no.

468
00:39:02,664 --> 00:39:04,640
It's not that at all. But...

469
00:39:04,640 --> 00:39:06,783
<i>He must be joking, right?</i>

470
00:39:06,783 --> 00:39:09,116
I'm not joking.

471
00:39:09,116 --> 00:39:10,816
I mean it.

472
00:39:17,232 --> 00:39:19,568
By the way, Assistant Manager Ki,
can you read minds or something?

473
00:39:19,568 --> 00:39:23,549
Se Ah, your thoughts
are written all over your face.

474
00:39:23,549 --> 00:39:26,283
That's why I like you even better.

475
00:39:32,764 --> 00:39:34,416
Oh, it's so nice here.

476
00:39:34,416 --> 00:39:37,316
The view is beautiful,
and it's so refreshing.

477
00:39:43,922 --> 00:39:46,565
Yeah.

478
00:39:55,444 --> 00:39:59,820
Why did he suddenly say, "I love you"?

479
00:39:59,820 --> 00:40:02,049
How many times have you even seen me?

480
00:40:03,272 --> 00:40:05,904
Is Assistant Manager Ki the kind of guy
who falls in love right away?

481
00:40:05,904 --> 00:40:08,349
He didn't seem like it, though.

482
00:40:08,349 --> 00:40:10,583
Well, wouldn't people normally say

483
00:40:10,583 --> 00:40:13,444
something like "I like you"

484
00:40:13,444 --> 00:40:19,308
or "Do you want to date me?" first?

485
00:40:19,308 --> 00:40:22,216
Well, I'd have to try it myself to know.

486
00:40:34,576 --> 00:40:36,292
That punk...

487
00:40:36,292 --> 00:40:39,896
Hey! You get a 30,000-won fine
for riding on the sidewalk!

488
00:40:39,896 --> 00:40:41,296
I caught you.

489
00:40:41,296 --> 00:40:43,549
I've seen your face!

490
00:41:09,068 --> 00:41:10,816
Have you eaten?

491
00:41:12,540 --> 00:41:15,728
I ate. Pizza and pasta.

492
00:41:15,728 --> 00:41:17,764
Good job.

493
00:41:17,764 --> 00:41:20,332
Oh, why were you
spacing out like that earlier?

494
00:41:20,332 --> 00:41:22,049
Did something happen?

495
00:41:23,064 --> 00:41:26,149
No, nothing.

496
00:41:28,740 --> 00:41:30,440
Want to go play some games?

497
00:41:31,952 --> 00:41:34,516
- No.
- Want to go get some chicken feet?

498
00:41:36,644 --> 00:41:38,344
No.

499
00:41:38,984 --> 00:41:40,396
Why?

500
00:41:40,396 --> 00:41:41,860
Because I like you?

501
00:41:41,860 --> 00:41:44,812
Hey, don't say things like that.

502
00:41:44,812 --> 00:41:46,616
It's making me uncomfortable.

503
00:41:54,386 --> 00:41:56,086
Kwon Se Ah.

504
00:41:57,928 --> 00:41:59,936
I do like you,

505
00:41:59,936 --> 00:42:02,949
but these are just my feelings.

506
00:42:02,949 --> 00:42:05,916
Of course, I respect
whatever you feel toward me.

507
00:42:05,916 --> 00:42:11,349
The time I've spent with you
and our friendship mean a lot to me.

508
00:42:11,349 --> 00:42:15,183
If you meet someone you like,
I'll let go of my feelings.

509
00:42:16,408 --> 00:42:20,424
Until then, I'll just keep feeling this way.

510
00:42:20,424 --> 00:42:24,183
So can't you just hang out with me today?

511
00:42:25,763 --> 00:42:30,749
Hey, I'd be really hurt if this
made things awkward between us.

512
00:42:35,072 --> 00:42:37,520
Oh, say something.

513
00:42:37,520 --> 00:42:41,349
You have to tell me
what you're thinking for me to know.

514
00:42:47,864 --> 00:42:49,780
Okay.

515
00:42:49,780 --> 00:42:55,283
But if you say something like "I like you"
one more time, I'm going to kill you.

516
00:42:56,172 --> 00:42:57,872
Okay!

517
00:42:59,604 --> 00:43:01,440
Let's go.

518
00:43:01,440 --> 00:43:02,552
Don't do that.

519
00:43:02,552 --> 00:43:03,700
Where? Let's go!

520
00:43:03,700 --> 00:43:04,783
Let's start with the PC bang.

521
00:43:04,783 --> 00:43:06,516
Good.

522
00:43:12,349 --> 00:43:14,552
Oh, Mr. Jo. What's up this early?

523
00:43:14,552 --> 00:43:17,348
Sir, that woman who's your friend's wife...

524
00:43:17,348 --> 00:43:20,688
The one who caught those voice-phishing
scammers herself last time.

525
00:43:20,688 --> 00:43:22,392
<i>What does she do for a living?</i>

526
00:43:22,392 --> 00:43:23,572
Ms. Bo Na?

527
00:43:23,572 --> 00:43:25,536
She's just an ordinary office worker. Why?

528
00:43:25,536 --> 00:43:29,120
Wow. I thought she worked in
action or something.

529
00:43:29,120 --> 00:43:30,640
She's quite the joker, huh?

530
00:43:30,640 --> 00:43:34,388
What those scammers said
about her was actually true?

531
00:43:34,388 --> 00:43:36,216
Just send it over for now.

532
00:43:42,892 --> 00:43:45,376
So he just jumped over those buildings?

533
00:43:45,376 --> 00:43:47,549
What, did he fly?

534
00:43:49,660 --> 00:43:52,064
What a lunatic.

535
00:43:52,064 --> 00:43:54,649
What on earth are you thinking?

536
00:44:19,384 --> 00:44:23,083
Are you finished already?
Or did you not even start?

537
00:44:29,816 --> 00:44:33,000
Why'd you leave your job, Team Leader?

538
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:35,428
All of a sudden? Come on.

539
00:44:35,428 --> 00:44:38,060
I told you before.

540
00:44:38,060 --> 00:44:41,100
I was exhausted physically and emotionally
after divorcing the kids' dad,

541
00:44:41,100 --> 00:44:43,149
and I lost the will to work.

542
00:44:43,149 --> 00:44:47,716
People change when life takes a major turn.

543
00:44:49,920 --> 00:44:51,916
I didn't believe you back then, either.

544
00:44:53,556 --> 00:44:56,083
But was there really no other reason?

545
00:45:02,212 --> 00:45:04,516
Because my husband found out.

546
00:45:05,684 --> 00:45:07,849
What I was really doing.

547
00:45:08,556 --> 00:45:13,140
He told me to quit immediately
and disappear somewhere far away.

548
00:45:13,140 --> 00:45:16,749
And never show my face
in front of the family again.

549
00:45:17,708 --> 00:45:19,392
In return, he said he'd keep it a secret

550
00:45:19,392 --> 00:45:20,949
from the kids for the rest of their lives.

551
00:45:22,152 --> 00:45:24,036
Sure, I said yes.

552
00:45:24,036 --> 00:45:27,283
What else could I do? I'm their mom.

553
00:45:27,283 --> 00:45:29,583
I have to protect my kids.

554
00:45:34,144 --> 00:45:36,883
Why are you suddenly asking that?

555
00:45:38,228 --> 00:45:41,049
So an unavoidable variable
popped up with your husband, huh?

556
00:45:41,049 --> 00:45:44,349
Is this about him coming by last time?

557
00:45:47,464 --> 00:45:49,449
I'm not sure.

558
00:45:50,348 --> 00:45:52,716
I want to ask, but I can't bring myself to.

559
00:45:56,632 --> 00:45:59,176
You're worrying in advance

560
00:45:59,176 --> 00:46:02,683
because you're afraid of
what the answer might be, right?

561
00:46:07,949 --> 00:46:11,683
Not every story ends the same way.

562
00:46:11,683 --> 00:46:16,183
Besides, he's your husband, and he cares
about you more than anyone else.

563
00:46:17,012 --> 00:46:19,049
That's not like you.

564
00:46:19,748 --> 00:46:22,983
You're not the type to worry in advance.

565
00:46:30,582 --> 00:46:32,409
- Oh, you're here?
- Yeah.

566
00:46:32,409 --> 00:46:35,391
About Oh Seung Ah, you asked me
to look into, she changed her name.

567
00:46:35,391 --> 00:46:36,783
Changed it? To what?

568
00:46:36,783 --> 00:46:38,148
Oh Hyun Nam.

569
00:46:38,148 --> 00:46:39,896
[Personal Information]
This is her current ID photo.

570
00:46:39,896 --> 00:46:42,007
Her current address is
Hanan-ro in Yangpyeong-gu.

571
00:46:42,007 --> 00:46:43,872
And she seems to have a decent job too.

572
00:46:43,872 --> 00:46:45,136
Where does she work?

573
00:46:45,136 --> 00:46:47,183
Durumi Electronics?

574
00:46:49,483 --> 00:46:53,283
[Oh Hyun Nam,
Durumi Electronics Sales Team 3]

575
00:47:03,896 --> 00:47:07,483
I put the advice you gave me to good use.

576
00:47:09,216 --> 00:47:11,268
The advice I gave you?

577
00:47:11,268 --> 00:47:12,968
Oh.

578
00:47:13,824 --> 00:47:15,849
How long have you two been dating?

579
00:47:16,540 --> 00:47:18,240
What?

580
00:47:19,212 --> 00:47:23,783
You didn't use it on some woman
you'd barely even met, did you?

581
00:47:27,496 --> 00:47:31,483
Good grief, only a lunatic would do that.

582
00:47:32,944 --> 00:47:34,644
Jeez.

583
00:47:45,592 --> 00:47:47,583
Do you have anything to say?

584
00:47:49,356 --> 00:47:52,249
I was just going to get something to drink.

585
00:47:52,960 --> 00:47:54,660
Okay.

586
00:48:02,636 --> 00:48:05,828
Excuse me, who... are you?

587
00:48:05,828 --> 00:48:07,756
Oh, my!

588
00:48:07,756 --> 00:48:09,956
Tae Min.

589
00:48:09,956 --> 00:48:11,372
Are you crazy?

590
00:48:11,372 --> 00:48:14,040
Are you dating someone?

591
00:48:14,040 --> 00:48:15,432
Hey!

592
00:48:15,432 --> 00:48:19,083
Wow, this is so unfamiliar. Very unfamiliar.

593
00:48:23,212 --> 00:48:25,316
Hey, this place has changed a little.

594
00:48:29,188 --> 00:48:31,016
Did you take a shower?

595
00:48:33,844 --> 00:48:35,544
Huh?

596
00:48:36,940 --> 00:48:39,083
And what's with your hair...

597
00:48:39,954 --> 00:48:41,654
Hey!

598
00:48:48,256 --> 00:48:49,628
Is everything all right now?

599
00:48:49,628 --> 00:48:51,460
Yeah.

600
00:48:51,460 --> 00:48:52,808
Yul's doing better now.

601
00:48:52,808 --> 00:48:56,183
No, I mean you.
You've never been like that before.

602
00:49:00,020 --> 00:49:01,720
Well...

603
00:49:03,656 --> 00:49:05,320
Maybe it's because I'm a mom now?

604
00:49:05,320 --> 00:49:07,449
If that's all it is, that's a relief.

605
00:49:08,783 --> 00:49:12,383
You... Why did you follow me back then?

606
00:49:21,260 --> 00:49:23,383
Take me with you too.

607
00:49:24,476 --> 00:49:26,748
I didn't get my slingshot back then.

608
00:49:26,748 --> 00:49:29,636
When I came to Korea, why did you follow me?

609
00:49:29,636 --> 00:49:31,749
Because Yoo Bo Na was going.

610
00:49:34,556 --> 00:49:36,216
Then...

611
00:49:37,072 --> 00:49:39,416
if I leave again someday,

612
00:49:40,200 --> 00:49:42,216
will you follow me then too?

613
00:49:43,640 --> 00:49:45,340
Are you going somewhere?

614
00:49:53,572 --> 00:49:55,649
Where would I even go?

615
00:49:55,649 --> 00:49:57,583
Everything I need is right here.

616
00:50:00,516 --> 00:50:03,752
Any update on that punk?

617
00:50:03,752 --> 00:50:05,232
Nothing much.

618
00:50:05,232 --> 00:50:07,216
What's up? Is something happening?

619
00:50:16,168 --> 00:50:19,716
No. I guess I'm just being sensitive.

620
00:50:20,820 --> 00:50:23,716
Please check his main routes and let me know.

621
00:50:23,716 --> 00:50:26,080
[Chief's Office]

622
00:50:26,080 --> 00:50:29,920
What's gotten into you?
Why have you been so out of it lately?

623
00:50:29,920 --> 00:50:31,576
Is something going on?

624
00:50:31,576 --> 00:50:33,968
No. Nothing like that.

625
00:50:33,968 --> 00:50:36,164
That's the problem.

626
00:50:36,164 --> 00:50:38,564
Can you have nothing going on?
Of course, you can't.

627
00:50:38,564 --> 00:50:40,180
You should have plenty going on.

628
00:50:40,180 --> 00:50:43,083
It's been ages since the Kingfisher
task force was launched.

629
00:50:43,083 --> 00:50:45,248
You should have something
to show for it by now.

630
00:50:45,248 --> 00:50:47,772
Me? Show what?

631
00:50:47,772 --> 00:50:49,508
What do you mean, "what"?

632
00:50:49,508 --> 00:50:52,383
Who Kingfisher is, how old he is,
where he lives, what he does.

633
00:50:52,383 --> 00:50:53,996
Why should I?

634
00:50:53,996 --> 00:50:56,848
Why me? There are loads of reporters around.

635
00:50:56,848 --> 00:50:59,628
Why should I be the one doing that?

636
00:50:59,628 --> 00:51:04,549
You've devoted years to chasing Kingfisher.
Why are you getting mad?

637
00:51:08,576 --> 00:51:13,024
I hear this task force
is different from the previous ones.

638
00:51:13,024 --> 00:51:16,212
Everyone's closing in, thinking they
might actually get something this time.

639
00:51:16,212 --> 00:51:18,949
Do you want to end up doing nothing
but transcribing everyone else's work?

640
00:51:21,172 --> 00:51:24,592
Those Kingfisher articles
you've written over the years.

641
00:51:24,592 --> 00:51:28,868
They offer a different depth
and perspective. I like them!

642
00:51:28,868 --> 00:51:31,704
Honestly, your articles were pretty
sympathetic toward Kingfisher, weren't they?

643
00:51:31,704 --> 00:51:33,848
And you're just going to
sit on the sidelines now?

644
00:51:33,848 --> 00:51:38,116
You're really going to let everyone say
whatever they want about Kingfisher?

645
00:52:00,549 --> 00:52:01,816
[Kwon Tae Seong]

646
00:52:01,816 --> 00:52:04,449
[Kingfisher, Search Results]

647
00:52:05,883 --> 00:52:09,583
[If I Ever Meet Kingfisher]

648
00:52:13,983 --> 00:52:18,383
[If I Ever Meet Kingfisher]

649
00:52:21,996 --> 00:52:23,537
<i>What kind of person</i>

650
00:52:23,537 --> 00:52:26,816
<i>would devote their entire life
to something like that?</i>

651
00:52:28,684 --> 00:52:30,612
<i>But I didn't.</i>

652
00:52:30,612 --> 00:52:34,516
<i>I never carelessly speculated about him.</i>

653
00:52:34,516 --> 00:52:37,504
<i>So even if Kingfisher's identity
is revealed someday,</i>

654
00:52:37,504 --> 00:52:39,749
<i>I won't be surprised.</i>

655
00:52:40,368 --> 00:52:44,424
<i>I'll simply look forward to the day
I finally meet him.</i>

656
00:52:44,424 --> 00:52:47,883
<i>I want to sit beside him by the campfire</i>

657
00:52:47,883 --> 00:52:50,483
<i>and listen to him talk about
his life all night.</i>

658
00:52:51,244 --> 00:52:55,483
<i>Without asking anything,
I could simply listen.</i>

659
00:53:02,852 --> 00:53:06,916
<i>But if I were to meet him as
an ordinary citizen rather than a reporter,</i>

660
00:53:06,916 --> 00:53:11,328
<i>I'd have a legal duty
to report him to the police.</i>

661
00:53:11,328 --> 00:53:13,316
<i>Could I do that?</i>

662
00:53:14,183 --> 00:53:16,349
<i>Can I actually turn him in?</i>

663
00:53:17,316 --> 00:53:22,883
<i>To that question,
I haven't found an answer yet.</i>

664
00:53:22,883 --> 00:53:25,183
Will you report it to the police?

665
00:53:26,949 --> 00:53:32,016
Oh, since you're a reporter,
are you going to expose her in an article?

666
00:53:32,996 --> 00:53:36,049
Did you do that to me that day
because you were afraid I'd do that?

667
00:53:36,800 --> 00:53:40,583
If that was the case, I wouldn't
have just put you to sleep.

668
00:53:43,874 --> 00:53:47,824
Well, let's just say I changed my mind.

669
00:53:47,824 --> 00:53:49,064
Because I got curious.

670
00:53:49,064 --> 00:53:53,092
About what exactly Yoo Bo Na
is trying to protect.

671
00:53:53,092 --> 00:53:54,983
And whether she'll be

672
00:53:55,683 --> 00:53:58,816
able to keep protecting it.

673
00:53:58,816 --> 00:54:00,616
What do you mean?

674
00:54:00,616 --> 00:54:04,083
It's probably the same kind of thing?

675
00:54:04,083 --> 00:54:09,760
The reason you wanted to
keep your promise to me.

676
00:54:09,760 --> 00:54:14,049
Oh, by the way, Yoo Bo Na
doesn't know about that day, right?

677
00:54:14,049 --> 00:54:18,248
That's why I'm still alive and well.

678
00:54:18,248 --> 00:54:22,583
Isn't it probably the same thing?

679
00:54:22,583 --> 00:54:25,483
The reason why you had to

680
00:54:25,483 --> 00:54:29,416
remain in the dark about Yoo Bo Na.

681
00:54:32,149 --> 00:54:38,549
"What matters is the present, not the past."
You once said it, right?

682
00:54:39,649 --> 00:54:44,849
Yoo Bo Na was Yoo Bo Na in the past,
and she's still Yoo Bo Na now.

683
00:54:44,849 --> 00:54:48,532
What's left is your choice, isn't it?

684
00:54:48,532 --> 00:54:51,283
Whether you go with her or leave her behind.

685
00:54:51,283 --> 00:54:55,683
Including reporting or exposing her
in an article, of course.

686
00:55:00,249 --> 00:55:04,983
[Durumi Electronics]

687
00:55:16,980 --> 00:55:18,680
Ms. Oh Hyun Nam!

688
00:55:29,532 --> 00:55:31,883
Don't you want some coffee?

689
00:55:37,008 --> 00:55:38,392
<i>Oh, excuse me!</i>

690
00:55:38,392 --> 00:55:40,316
I think you dropped something.

691
00:55:41,116 --> 00:55:43,283
Thank you.

692
00:56:09,724 --> 00:56:11,836
Why's there nowhere to park around here?

693
00:56:11,836 --> 00:56:13,749
What, isn't it here?

694
00:56:15,108 --> 00:56:17,672
Kingfisher's hiatus...

695
00:56:17,672 --> 00:56:20,883
What were the exact dates again?

696
00:56:22,688 --> 00:56:23,960
Grandma!

697
00:56:23,960 --> 00:56:25,560
Oh, my, look who's here!

698
00:56:25,560 --> 00:56:27,583
Yul is here.

699
00:56:28,892 --> 00:56:30,683
- You're here?
- Yes, Mother.

700
00:56:30,683 --> 00:56:31,924
Did you just get off work?

701
00:56:31,924 --> 00:56:34,652
Yeah, Yul wanted your fried chicken,
so I brought her.

702
00:56:34,652 --> 00:56:36,880
- Oh.
- Really?

703
00:56:36,880 --> 00:56:39,676
I'll fry you some really tasty chicken.

704
00:56:39,676 --> 00:56:41,376
Okay.

705
00:56:42,452 --> 00:56:43,576
Come sit down.

706
00:56:43,576 --> 00:56:45,276
Yes, Mother.

707
00:56:46,576 --> 00:56:48,776
Oh, Tae Seong's coming too, right?

708
00:56:48,776 --> 00:56:52,196
Oh, he's been pretty busy lately, Mother.

709
00:56:52,196 --> 00:56:55,288
I barely even see him myself.

710
00:56:55,288 --> 00:56:57,083
Really?

711
00:56:58,176 --> 00:56:59,500
I'll have it ready in no time.

712
00:56:59,500 --> 00:57:02,228
She's being unusually sweet.

713
00:57:02,228 --> 00:57:04,649
Is this the power of money?

714
00:57:07,788 --> 00:57:10,048
Yul, tear it up and eat it.

715
00:57:10,048 --> 00:57:12,636
Are things hard for you these days?

716
00:57:12,636 --> 00:57:15,716
You look really tired and stressed out.

717
00:57:15,716 --> 00:57:17,449
Well...

718
00:57:21,783 --> 00:57:27,620
Mother, Tae Seong hasn't said
anything unusual to you, has he?

719
00:57:27,620 --> 00:57:30,949
He hasn't really told me anything...

720
00:57:31,752 --> 00:57:33,496
Why? What's up with Tae Seong?

721
00:57:33,496 --> 00:57:36,516
Is Tae Seong cheating on you?

722
00:57:37,892 --> 00:57:39,860
Be careful what you say around the kid.

723
00:57:39,860 --> 00:57:42,320
You think he'd do something like that?

724
00:57:42,320 --> 00:57:45,088
I'm just kidding!

725
00:57:45,088 --> 00:57:48,204
- Yul, eat plenty.
- Okay.

726
00:57:49,920 --> 00:57:52,124
I'm not too sure, Mother.

727
00:57:52,124 --> 00:57:57,116
I just feel like Tae Seong's been
a little upset with me lately.

728
00:57:57,976 --> 00:58:01,496
What could he be upset with you about?

729
00:58:01,496 --> 00:58:03,568
I guess that time has come.

730
00:58:03,568 --> 00:58:08,140
That's why I quit working
when Hyeok Jun was five.

731
00:58:08,140 --> 00:58:13,583
My husband made such a fuss about me
putting work before our child and him...

732
00:58:14,928 --> 00:58:16,948
Then quit your job too.

733
00:58:16,948 --> 00:58:18,268
Mom!

734
00:58:18,268 --> 00:58:19,916
You're not exactly saving the world.

735
00:58:19,916 --> 00:58:23,676
What could possibly be more important
to a woman than her husband and child?

736
00:58:23,676 --> 00:58:26,349
Oh, Bo Na, don't take it to heart.

737
00:58:27,956 --> 00:58:29,983
There's one thing.

738
00:58:31,376 --> 00:58:32,983
My own life.

739
00:58:32,983 --> 00:58:35,808
I got married at 24

740
00:58:35,808 --> 00:58:40,216
and lived only for my husband and kids.

741
00:58:40,216 --> 00:58:43,920
Then when Tae Seong's dad
suddenly passed away, I felt so lost.

742
00:58:43,920 --> 00:58:47,849
I needed to make a living,
but I didn't know how to do anything.

743
00:58:47,849 --> 00:58:51,440
So I scraped together what I had
and opened this place.

744
00:58:51,440 --> 00:58:54,849
At first, I was embarrassed
to be frying chicken.

745
00:58:54,849 --> 00:58:57,307
Oil splashed everywhere, my skin got burned,

746
00:58:57,307 --> 00:59:00,449
and I had to deal with drunk customers.

747
00:59:00,449 --> 00:59:02,216
Good grief.

748
00:59:03,672 --> 00:59:06,440
I cried a lot too.

749
00:59:06,440 --> 00:59:08,104
Mom.

750
00:59:08,104 --> 00:59:10,483
But I came back to the shop the next day.

751
00:59:10,483 --> 00:59:12,116
I had to open the doors.

752
00:59:12,116 --> 00:59:15,216
No matter how hard it was, I kept showing up.

753
00:59:15,216 --> 00:59:18,836
And you know what? I came to like it.

754
00:59:18,836 --> 00:59:21,900
I was the owner of this shop.

755
00:59:21,900 --> 00:59:24,604
Frying chicken was my job.

756
00:59:24,604 --> 00:59:29,616
I realized, "Oh, this is my life."

757
00:59:36,360 --> 00:59:39,312
Working while raising a child isn't easy.

758
00:59:39,312 --> 00:59:40,964
But what can you do?

759
00:59:40,964 --> 00:59:42,904
Unless you absolutely hate what you do,

760
00:59:42,904 --> 00:59:46,783
if it's something you love,
you have to see it through.

761
00:59:48,940 --> 00:59:50,832
Oh, I completely forgot.

762
00:59:50,832 --> 00:59:53,549
I left a dishcloth boiling on the stove.

763
00:59:55,856 --> 00:59:58,080
When you're both busy, bring Yul here.

764
00:59:58,080 --> 01:00:01,149
I'll watch her,
even if I have to close the shop.

765
01:00:03,056 --> 01:00:05,216
And pay me for the day's work.

766
01:00:06,680 --> 01:00:08,740
Didn't you say you'd never close up,
no matter what?

767
01:00:08,740 --> 01:00:10,849
You changed your tune pretty fast, huh?

768
01:00:19,216 --> 01:00:21,556
Mommy, catch me if you can!

769
01:00:21,556 --> 01:00:22,940
Yul!

770
01:00:22,940 --> 01:00:25,620
Oh, you're too fast. I can't catch you.

771
01:00:25,620 --> 01:00:26,883
- What should we do next then?
- Mommy!

772
01:00:26,883 --> 01:00:30,516
- I want to do that!
- Okay, go on up. You're good at that.

773
01:00:30,516 --> 01:00:32,749
Watch your head.

774
01:00:32,749 --> 01:00:34,949
Wow.

775
01:00:34,949 --> 01:00:36,696
Wow, you're good!

776
01:00:36,696 --> 01:00:40,600
I actually don't really like
strawberry shakes.

777
01:00:40,600 --> 01:00:45,036
But when I fell in love,
I really wanted to do that.

778
01:00:45,036 --> 01:00:47,752
Sitting across from each other
and drinking strawberry shakes.

779
01:00:47,752 --> 01:00:50,549
<i>Because that's the kind of
person you are to me.</i>

780
01:00:53,752 --> 01:00:55,816
You're going higher!

781
01:00:55,816 --> 01:00:57,772
Mommy, I want to do that.

782
01:00:57,772 --> 01:00:59,736
Okay.

783
01:00:59,736 --> 01:01:01,256
Can you get up on your own, Yul?

784
01:01:01,256 --> 01:01:03,356
- Yeah, I can get up.
- Go ahead. Stand up.

785
01:01:03,356 --> 01:01:06,136
Oh, let's see.

786
01:01:06,136 --> 01:01:07,936
Your hand looks okay. Right?

787
01:01:07,936 --> 01:01:11,516
Does it hurt? You're bleeding a little, Yul.

788
01:01:11,516 --> 01:01:13,249
[A Band-Aid]

789
01:01:15,116 --> 01:01:16,816
Does it hurt?

790
01:01:23,336 --> 01:01:26,183
With this on,
it'll get better in no time, right?

791
01:01:26,183 --> 01:01:27,883
Yeah.

792
01:01:29,684 --> 01:01:31,660
Wow, it really stuck on well.

793
01:01:31,660 --> 01:01:33,216
Did it stick?

794
01:01:33,216 --> 01:01:34,916
Yeah.

795
01:01:36,316 --> 01:01:38,188
Huh? It's Daddy!

796
01:01:38,188 --> 01:01:40,720
Daddy!

797
01:01:40,720 --> 01:01:42,908
My little precious!

798
01:01:42,908 --> 01:01:44,352
- Did you have fun?
- Yeah.

799
01:01:44,352 --> 01:01:45,616
What did you do?

800
01:01:45,616 --> 01:01:46,968
I went on the swings too.

801
01:01:46,968 --> 01:01:49,116
You're back early today.

802
01:01:49,116 --> 01:01:51,480
Yeah, I finished early.

803
01:01:51,480 --> 01:01:53,768
What about dinner?

804
01:01:53,768 --> 01:01:55,716
Well, not yet.

805
01:01:56,416 --> 01:01:58,264
Let's go home. I'll whip up
something tasty for you.

806
01:01:58,264 --> 01:01:59,964
Okay.

807
01:02:09,860 --> 01:02:11,616
Even right now, Kingfisher could be

808
01:02:11,616 --> 01:02:15,580
sitting at a dinner table
looking completely ordinary.

809
01:02:15,580 --> 01:02:21,304
A diligent employee,
someone's spouse, or a loving parent.

810
01:02:21,304 --> 01:02:25,681
He could've gotten married,
started a family, and had kids, like me.

811
01:02:25,681 --> 01:02:28,043
- Hey, you.
- Hey, who knows?

812
01:02:28,043 --> 01:02:30,996
That sticker might really have been a clue.

813
01:02:30,996 --> 01:02:33,216
<i>You never know.</i>

814
01:02:36,349 --> 01:02:37,936
[Headband, Red Devil, Tall and Slender]

815
01:02:37,936 --> 01:02:39,516
[Short or Tied Hair, Big Bag on Shoulder]

816
01:02:51,788 --> 01:02:53,549
Who is it?

817
01:03:09,484 --> 01:03:10,900
What brings you here at this hour,
out of the blue?

818
01:03:10,900 --> 01:03:13,949
I happened to be nearby,
so I stopped in to see Yul.

819
01:03:14,796 --> 01:03:17,248
Yul, Mr. Dong Jin is here!

820
01:03:17,248 --> 01:03:19,364
Mr. Lee!

821
01:03:19,364 --> 01:03:23,483
Oh, Yul. There's my Yul.

822
01:03:23,483 --> 01:03:26,468
Yul, how old are you?

823
01:03:26,468 --> 01:03:31,260
- Four.
- That's right, four.

824
01:03:31,260 --> 01:03:32,820
Dong Jin, you're here?

825
01:03:32,820 --> 01:03:34,220
Oh, yes.

826
01:03:34,220 --> 01:03:36,149
Sorry for dropping by without calling.

827
01:03:36,149 --> 01:03:38,948
- Not at all.
- I already had dinner.

828
01:03:38,948 --> 01:03:41,716
Grab some tea and fruit. Come on in.

829
01:04:02,164 --> 01:04:05,236
Why are you just standing there? Sit down.

830
01:04:05,236 --> 01:04:09,488
- When did you say you first met Bo Na?
- Huh?

831
01:04:09,488 --> 01:04:11,199
Eight years ago, during the World Cup.

832
01:04:11,199 --> 01:04:13,888
When you had your head cracked open
and were in the hospital, right?

833
01:04:13,888 --> 01:04:16,876
Why are you suddenly
asking about my love life?

834
01:04:16,876 --> 01:04:19,080
Are you lonely these days?

835
01:04:19,080 --> 01:04:21,116
Mr. Lee, look at this.

836
01:04:21,956 --> 01:04:24,120
Oh, Yul!

837
01:04:24,120 --> 01:04:27,529
Wow, you put stickers on your doll?

838
01:04:27,529 --> 01:04:29,183
Wow.

839
01:04:34,112 --> 01:04:36,860
It's a Baby Shark sticker!

840
01:04:36,860 --> 01:04:39,216
You like Baby Shark, don't you, Yul?

841
01:04:39,216 --> 01:04:41,016
Yeah, I do.

842
01:04:42,016 --> 01:04:44,684
Come on, what kid doesn't
like that these days?

843
01:04:44,684 --> 01:04:48,996
Just like you said, every home in the country
with a toddler has tons of them.

844
01:04:48,996 --> 01:04:50,696
Yeah.

845
01:04:51,548 --> 01:04:53,364
Dong Jin, have some fruit.

846
01:04:53,364 --> 01:04:55,064
Oh, thank you.

847
01:05:01,428 --> 01:05:02,972
Are you still busy these days?

848
01:05:02,972 --> 01:05:04,312
Well, yes.

849
01:05:04,312 --> 01:05:07,749
I joined the Kingfisher task force.

850
01:05:07,749 --> 01:05:10,249
Oh, then you must be really busy.

851
01:05:10,249 --> 01:05:12,156
Well, it's just...

852
01:05:12,156 --> 01:05:16,056
You returned to work after taking
three years of parental leave, right?

853
01:05:16,056 --> 01:05:18,136
Have you adjusted okay?

854
01:05:18,136 --> 01:05:21,168
Well, yeah. Everything's fine.

855
01:05:21,168 --> 01:05:25,349
She's been back at work for ages.
Mind your own business, man.

856
01:05:28,868 --> 01:05:31,983
Well, you know Gu Jong Ryeol, right?

857
01:05:32,732 --> 01:05:34,096
Gu Jong Ryeol?

858
01:05:34,096 --> 01:05:36,480
- Yeah.
- Oh, yeah.

859
01:05:36,480 --> 01:05:38,204
I saw the article.

860
01:05:38,204 --> 01:05:39,949
I have a feeling...

861
01:05:40,704 --> 01:05:43,449
that it was the work of Kingfisher.

862
01:05:46,860 --> 01:05:50,216
Yul, do you want some fruit?

863
01:05:52,076 --> 01:05:53,776
Here you go.

864
01:05:54,783 --> 01:05:58,349
There were severe signs of
blunt-force trauma on his face.

865
01:05:58,349 --> 01:06:02,036
But Kingfisher has never physically
touched his victims before.

866
01:06:02,036 --> 01:06:05,136
You know him better than anyone.
You're the Kingfisher expert.

867
01:06:05,136 --> 01:06:07,100
What are you doing talking about work here?

868
01:06:07,100 --> 01:06:08,740
Have some fruit. It's good.

869
01:06:08,740 --> 01:06:10,836
Alright.

870
01:06:10,836 --> 01:06:14,740
The profiler said there was emotion involved.

871
01:06:14,740 --> 01:06:19,316
If he beat him that brutally,
there had to be anger behind it.

872
01:06:20,283 --> 01:06:22,896
The kid can hear you. Stop.

873
01:06:22,896 --> 01:06:24,783
Well, it just made me

874
01:06:25,396 --> 01:06:27,616
think of something.

875
01:06:28,683 --> 01:06:33,183
Could Kingfisher be a parent raising a child?

876
01:06:35,049 --> 01:06:36,788
Mommy, have one of these.

877
01:06:36,788 --> 01:06:38,488
Okay.

878
01:06:40,208 --> 01:06:42,712
Yul, do you like apples better?

879
01:06:42,712 --> 01:06:44,188
You said it yourself.

880
01:06:44,188 --> 01:06:47,583
He could've gotten married and had a child.
You never know.

881
01:06:49,592 --> 01:06:51,384
Finished your tea?

882
01:06:51,384 --> 01:06:53,216
Let's step outside.

883
01:07:01,332 --> 01:07:03,483
Do you have something to say to me?

884
01:07:04,416 --> 01:07:06,916
Say it. Stop beating around the bush.
What is it?

885
01:07:09,920 --> 01:07:12,116
Are you in league with Kingfisher?

886
01:07:14,272 --> 01:07:17,649
What kind of nonsense
have you been spouting lately?

887
01:07:17,649 --> 01:07:21,316
The person you said you had to
protect with that embargo,

888
01:07:22,328 --> 01:07:24,028
is it Kingfisher?

889
01:07:26,508 --> 01:07:31,168
<i>To that question,
I haven't found an answer yet.</i>

890
01:07:31,168 --> 01:07:34,549
No, I'm on your side.

891
01:07:38,252 --> 01:07:40,342
I'm being serious.

892
01:07:40,342 --> 01:07:44,668
That man I saw before,
he really is Kingfisher.

893
01:07:44,668 --> 01:07:46,064
On the day of the Haegong-dong incident,

894
01:07:46,064 --> 01:07:49,384
I tailed Yeon Chang Bok's mom
and found where Yeon Chang Bok was hiding.

895
01:07:49,384 --> 01:07:53,300
I searched the nearby rooftops, spotted
Kingfisher taking aim, and got caught.

896
01:07:53,300 --> 01:07:56,104
Hey, why are you only telling me this now?

897
01:07:56,104 --> 01:07:59,116
Because he threatened to harm my family.

898
01:07:59,752 --> 01:08:03,649
Then the person you said
you had to protect...

899
01:08:03,649 --> 01:08:07,416
My wife and my child. My beloved family.

900
01:08:08,336 --> 01:08:10,116
I need to protect them.

901
01:08:14,640 --> 01:08:16,449
You'll be on my side, right?

902
01:08:17,176 --> 01:08:19,048
Huh?

903
01:08:19,048 --> 01:08:21,116
You said you wanted to repay the favor.

904
01:08:40,540 --> 01:08:42,292
Did you see him off okay?

905
01:08:42,292 --> 01:08:44,716
Yul fell asleep.

906
01:08:46,256 --> 01:08:49,183
I'll clean up. You go wash up first, honey.

907
01:08:59,392 --> 01:09:01,092
What's wrong?

908
01:09:17,268 --> 01:09:22,016
I'm done with everything busy now.
Want to take Yul out this weekend?

909
01:09:26,248 --> 01:09:27,948
I'd love to.

910
01:09:52,912 --> 01:09:55,208
Yul, look at Daddy.

911
01:09:55,208 --> 01:09:56,908
Daddy!

912
01:09:58,152 --> 01:09:59,949
Look at Daddy.

913
01:10:14,628 --> 01:10:16,683
Mommy, hello!

914
01:10:19,224 --> 01:10:20,924
Be careful!

915
01:10:22,984 --> 01:10:24,684
Got you.

916
01:10:30,488 --> 01:10:33,316
Mommy's taking a picture! Look at Mommy!

917
01:10:36,452 --> 01:10:38,152
Yul!

918
01:10:50,012 --> 01:10:52,130
- Oh, dear...
- Sir, let me help you with that.

919
01:10:52,130 --> 01:10:54,730
Oh... Yes. Thank you.

920
01:11:04,952 --> 01:11:07,108
It's super yummy.

921
01:11:07,108 --> 01:11:08,924
- I love you.
- You love Mommy?

922
01:11:08,924 --> 01:11:09,924
I love you too.

923
01:11:09,924 --> 01:11:11,624
I love you too.

924
01:11:17,660 --> 01:11:18,983
Oh, thank you.

925
01:11:18,983 --> 01:11:20,916
- Yes.
- Thank you.

926
01:11:33,516 --> 01:11:35,249
Wait...

927
01:11:36,660 --> 01:11:38,783
Call an ambulance!

928
01:11:38,783 --> 01:11:40,483
What happened?

929
01:13:06,816 --> 01:13:09,372
What exactly is the point of all this?

930
01:13:09,372 --> 01:13:11,316
Kingfisher's social death?

931
01:13:11,316 --> 01:13:13,236
Is Kingfisher seriously insane?

932
01:13:13,236 --> 01:13:15,856
Why would he suddenly start killing people
who aren't even criminals?

933
01:13:15,856 --> 01:13:18,644
Isn't it possible the killer
isn't Kingfisher?

934
01:13:18,644 --> 01:13:20,049
Do you have evidence?

935
01:13:20,049 --> 01:13:21,468
We'll need to check that out from now on.

936
01:13:21,468 --> 01:13:25,512
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring him down.

937
01:13:25,512 --> 01:13:27,236
Bo Na, I can't find Yul!

938
01:13:27,236 --> 01:13:29,376
We have to catch them
before there's a third victim.

939
01:13:29,376 --> 01:13:32,636
I heard hair with matching DNA
was found at both shooting locations.

940
01:13:32,636 --> 01:13:34,349
We found it.
